  "aiConsentTitle": "Before you turn this on",
  "bulkAddModelHintLabel": "A model can read this for you",
  "bulkAddModelHintKeyLabel": "With your own API key",
  "aiConsentChangeProviderNote": "You can change provider later. Each provider's terms are shown in Settings, and nothing you type or photograph is sent until you use the feature.",
  "aiConsentOwnServerCheckNote": "Saving your server's address also asks it which models it offers, and runs one setup check \u2014 a fixed example line and a sample photograph of ours, never anything of yours.",
  "aiConsentAgreeLabel": "I UNDERSTAND",
  "aiAssistDisclosureCommon": "Your diary and your profile are never sent. Nutrition values always come from the food databases, never from the model. The key is stored on this device only: EatPoint never sees it and does not pay for its use.",
  "aiAssistDisclosureAnthropic": "With a key saved, the text you type on the multi-item add screen — and any photo you choose to read there — is sent to Anthropic. Photos are sent for that one request and never saved.",
  "aiAssistDisclosureOpenRouter": "With a key saved, the text you type on the multi-item add screen — and any photo you choose to read there — is sent to OpenRouter, which forwards it to the provider serving your chosen model. OpenRouter also forwards an account-level identity to that provider on every request, and this cannot be switched off. It does not keep your content beyond routing the request, except as required for abuse detection, security, billing or legal compliance. The vendor serving your model keeps what it receives under its own policy.",
  "aiAssistDisclosureOpenAI": "With a key saved, the text you type on the multi-item add screen — and any photo you choose to read there — is sent to OpenAI. OpenAI keeps what you send for up to 30 days to monitor for abuse, and longer if the law requires it or it is reasonably necessary to protect its services or a third party from harm.",
  "aiAssistProviderOwnServerLabel": "Your own server",
  "aiAssistEndpointFieldLabel": "Server address",
  "aiAssistModelFieldLabel": "Model name",
  "aiAssistDisclosureOwnServerSecure": "With an address saved, the text you type on the multi-item add screen, and any photo you choose to read there, is sent to {host} — a server you run. No third party receives it, and the project has no relationship with that machine and can promise nothing about what it keeps. The connection is encrypted.",
  "@aiAssistDisclosureOwnServerSecure": {"placeholders": {"host": {"type": "String"}}},
  "aiAssistDisclosureOwnServerPlaintext": "With an address saved, the text you type on the multi-item add screen, and any photo you choose to read there, is sent to {host} — a server you run. No third party receives it, and the project has no relationship with that machine and can promise nothing about what it keeps. This address is plain HTTP, so the connection is not encrypted: anything on the network between this phone and that server can read what is sent.",
  "@aiAssistDisclosureOwnServerPlaintext": {"placeholders": {"host": {"type": "String"}}},
  "aiAssistDisclosureOwnServerGemini": "With an address saved, the text you type on the multi-item add screen, and any photo you choose to read there, is sent to Google's Gemini API at {host}. This is not a server you run: Google receives it, and the project has no relationship with Google. On unpaid Gemini API use, Google may use what you send to improve its products and machine learning, and human reviewers may read it. On paid use, and on all use in the EEA, Switzerland and the UK, Google does not use it to improve its products, but logs it for a limited time to detect misuse.",
  "@aiAssistDisclosureOwnServerGemini": {"placeholders": {"host": {"type": "String"}}},
